<div class="help-article">
    <p class="help-lead">
        <a href="transactions">Transactions</a> lists everything you've imported. Filter it down to what you're after, fix
        categories, tags and tax treatments row by row, or change the whole filtered list in one go.
    </p>

    <h3>Filters</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>From</strong> and <strong>To</strong>: the dates to show.</li>
        <li><strong>Accounts</strong>: tick any number; none ticked means all. Remembered for next time.</li>
        <li><strong>Category</strong>: a top-level category includes all its details; pick a detail for just that one.</li>
        <li><strong>Tags</strong>: transactions with any of the picked tags.</li>
        <li><strong>Tax treatment</strong>: transactions marked for a tax category, such as Medical expenses.</li>
        <li><strong>Category review</strong>: <em>Needs review</em> shows the automatic categories you haven't confirmed yet.</li>
        <li><strong>Search</strong>: words in the description. Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> or click away to apply it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        The line above the table counts what matches and totals the money in and out. Up to the newest 500 are shown; narrow the
        dates to see older ones. Click a column heading to sort by it, and again to reverse; the sort is remembered.
    </p>

    <h3>Changing one transaction</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Category</strong>: click it to open the category picker. See <a href="help?a=categorizing">Categories and review</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>✓</strong> beside an automatic category confirms it as it is.</li>
        <li><strong>+ Tag</strong>, under the description, adds a tag; the × on a tag removes it.</li>
        <li><strong>Tax</strong>: choose a tax category, or <em>Not claimable</em>. A suggested one shows ✓ to confirm it and ✕ to reject it.
            See <a href="help?a=tax-report">Tax report</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Changes save straight away; there's no Save button.</p>

    <h3>Changing the whole list</h3>
    <p>Above the table, three controls act on every transaction shown. Each asks before changing anything:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><span class="help-ui">Tag all … shown</span> adds, or removes, one tag on all of them.</li>
        <li><span class="help-ui">Set tax treatment of all … shown</span> marks all of them, for example every payment to your rental
            property's mortgage lender as a rental property expense.</li>
        <li><span class="help-ui">✓ Confirm … automatic categories</span> confirms every automatic category in the list as it is.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="help-note">
        A handy pattern: search for a merchant or a lender, check the list is what you meant, then tag it or set its tax
        treatment all at once.
    </p>
</div>
